rconnect-nccl#planes","content":"Typical names"},"3355":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-18","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"Carries"},"3356":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-19","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"LAN / management"},"3357":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-20","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"RJ-45 10GbE, often `enP7s7`"},"3358":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-21","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"K3s, SSH, dashboard, LiteLLM, NCCL bootstrap / Gloo"},"3359":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-22","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"High-speed"},"3360":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-23","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"ConnectX-7 QSFP"},"3361":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-24","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"NCCL payload / tensor-parallel all-reduce"},"3362":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-25","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#planes","content":"K3s/Flannel stay on the LAN. Do not put Kubernetes on the QSFP nets."},"3363":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-26","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#1-node","content":"No inter-node NCCL. Local multi-GPU (if advertised) uses SHM/P2P. The `highspeed` inventory group is ignored."},"3364":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-27","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-dual-400g-aggregate","content":"Existing 1-node / 2-node Jobs and `group_vars` document:"},"3365":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-28","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-dual-400g-aggregate","content":"Also typically `NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_P2P_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_SHM_DISABLE=0`. Confirm names with `ibdev2netdev` on **your** nodes before baking env."},"3366":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-29","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#2-node-pair-dual-400g-aggregate","content":"kimi / kimi-test omit `hostNetwork` (isolation). Heavy Ray / GLM-5.2 Jobs set `hostNetwork: true` (and GLM `hostIPC: true`) so IFNAME is visible."},"3367":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-30","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"200 Gb/s per physical port — not 400G, not NVLink, not an IB switch. Triangle:"},"3368":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-31","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Port0 = cage next to the RJ-45 jack; Port1 = far cage. Wrong polarity looks half-alive."},"3369":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-32","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Mode B (GLM-5.3-Flash TP=3) and Mode C (DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash TP=3) Jobs set:"},"3370":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-33","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Plus `hostNetwork: true` and `hostIPC: true`. If 10GbE is not `enP7s7`, set `LAB_MGMT_IFNAME`. Mode C also cuts `NCCL_BUFFSIZE=1MiB`."},"3371":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-34","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"`highspeed_interfaces: enp1s0f0np0,enp1s0f1np1` is the pair reference. Ring Jobs in `k8s/workloads/glm-5.3-flash/` and `deepseek-v4.1-flash/` already have the ring block."},"3372":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-35","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#3-node-qsfp-ring-mode-b-and-mode-c","content":"Full cabling, aliases, and util caps: LiteLLM rounded stack."},"3373":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-36","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"},"3374":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-37","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"**4 nodes:** one full port per node (`sfpplus1`…`sfpplus4`), 400G each."},"3375":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-38","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"**5 nodes:** three full ports + one port split with a breakout cable into\n`sfpplus4a` / `sfpplus4b` (two 200G lanes). Both lanes must be declared in the\n`switch.port_map` — the topology validator rejects a lone lane."},"3376":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-39","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"Each link is its own /24 (192.168.110–114, MTU 9000) from the generated per-node\nnetplan — one node per subnet, so there is no shared-suffix IP scheme to get wrong."},"3377":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-40","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` stays the management NIC; the payload rides the single RoCE HCA\n(`NCCL_IB_HCA` from live `ibdev2netdev` names per node)."},"3378":{"id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl-41","page_id":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl","tags":["nccl","interconnect","qsfp","mikrotik","safety","nvidia"],"type":"text","url":"/concepts/interconnect-nccl#4--5-nodes--mikrotik-crs804-4ddq-hrm-switch","content":"Heavy Jobs use `hostNetwork: true`. Do not assume the 2-node pair\n`NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME` list is complete — it is not, on a switch."